      statement: "The global --debug flag's help text says 'Enable debug logging (shows ripgrep vs Python fallback decisions, etc.)'. Either ripgrep-vs-Python decisions must produce debug output, or the help text must be updated to accurately describe what --debug does."  # c56f
      root_cause: "ranking.py contains the comment 'Note: ripgrep was tried here but removed due to complexity around regex' — ripgrep code path was removed but the --debug help text at cli.py:5741 still references it. Across 6 subcommands tested (catalog, sketch, config, test-coverage, search, cache-status), the --debug flag produces identical output to non-debug. Only 10 logger.debug calls exist in core, most for entry_point loading internals. Stale doc misleads users about flag scope."  # c56f
