  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): shares the \"help-text vs current behavior\" mechanic with WI-loloz (routes --help still documents deprecated -x/--exclude-tests no-op flag) and WI-figor (README implies --no-progress is general; only sketch/run accept it). All three are surfacing the absence of a doc-vs-impl gate over argparse help strings and README CLI examples. Suggest promoting to a META umbrella along the lines of \"CLI help text and README examples drift from argparse reality with no enforcement gate\". Code reference confirmed at cli.py:5741; the ripgrep path was removed but only the ranking.py:1599 comment and the cli.py:8069 internal comment survive — no live ripgrep dispatch."  # 0e02
